cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use crashmetrics in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "crashmetrics: Python tools for automotive crash engineering metrics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Voonna"
    given-names: "Satish Kumar"
version: "0.10.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vsk1729/crashmetrics"
url: "https://vsk1729.github.io/crashmetrics/"
abstract: >-
  Open-source Python package for automotive crash safety calculations:
  injury criteria (HIC, Nij, BrIC, DAMAGE, chest and leg criteria),
  Euro NCAP and Bharat NCAP scoring, pedestrian protection, AIS-100
  compliance checks, LS-DYNA energy checks, test-versus-CAE correlation
  (ISO/TS 18571, CORA) and feature extraction for machine learning.
keywords:
  - crashworthiness
  - crash safety
  - injury criteria
  - Euro NCAP
  - Bharat NCAP
  - pedestrian protection
  - LS-DYNA
  - CAE
